        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Calling All Dawns, Baba Yetu, Civilization IV\n- People: Christopher Tin, Jacqueline Horner-Kwiatek\n- Organizations: Anonymous 4, Grammy Awards\n\nFacts:\n- In 2005, the video game Civilization IV used “Baba Yetu” as its theme song.\n- Christopher Tin composed the song “Baba Yetu.”\n- At the 53rd Grammy Awards, Calling All Dawns won Best Classical Crossover Album.\n- At the 53rd Grammy Awards, “Baba Yetu” won Best Instrumental Arrangement Accompanying Vocalist(s).\n- Jacqueline Horner-Kwiatek is a member of the ensemble Anonymous 4.\n- Jacqueline Horner-Kwiatek was a featured soloist on Christopher Tin’s Grammy award-winning CD Calling All Dawns.",
